meta {
  name: Create Geo Exception (WFH period)
  type: http
  seq: 38
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/hr/geo-exceptions
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "user_id": "{{targetUserId}}",
    "exception_type": "wfh",
    "effective_from": "2026-01-01",
    "effective_to": "2026-01-31",
    "reason": "Approved work from home for January"
  }
}

docs {
  Date-bounded. Every punch in the window is recorded with is_wfh = true set
  SERVER-side, so the employee ticks nothing.

  Running this straight after Create-Geo-Exception-Remote must SUCCEED even
  though both cover the same user and dates: the no-overlap exclusion is scoped
  by exception_type. Running either one TWICE must fail with 409.
}
